--TEST--
an `extend` block may not extend a type its own package declares: a file with no package is the application, so a class in the same file is its own, and the help says to add the member to the class (`rule:classes/an-extend-block-adds-members-to-a-type`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
namespace Shop;

class Order {
    public int $total = 0;
}

extend Order as OrderTools {
    public function isEmpty(): bool {
        return $this->total == 0;
    }
}
// covers: lang:classes/extend-blocks
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0337]: `Shop\Order` is declared in your own code
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
